[38;5;231m⏺[39m I'm treating this as a bounded change: the page and its render loop already exist. So the design will be short and
  stay in this chat, with no spec file or plan document, and nothing gets built until you approve it.

  Where the filters go is a layout question, so I've sketched three options in a browser tab. It should have opened by
  itself; if not, it's at:
  [94m]8;id=vimfh1;http://localhost:62264/?key=0ee1829fcc6f452e7b6531c002b5532dd6fc20705fa9a3ddaa3312a31835dbf1\http://localhost:62264/?key=0ee1829fcc6f452e7b6531c002b5532dd6fc20705fa9a3ddaa3312a31835dbf1[39m]8;;\
  (The browser view uses a lot of tokens, so tell me if you'd rather stay in the terminal.)

  On screen, each option includes a "Showing X of Y events" count:
  - [1mA: Filter bar above the table.[0m Event type, date range and search are always visible, plus a "Clear filters" button.
  - [1mB: Filter button that opens a popover.[0m Active filters show as removable tags.
  - [1mC: Side panel with checkboxes,[0m to the left of the table.

  [1mI recommend A.[0m The main thing people need is to find a failed sign-in they don't recognize, and with A that filter is
  one click away. A also uses the existing Select, DatePicker and Search components as specified, and it wraps cleanly
  at 320px. B hides the filters behind an extra click and needs more JavaScript and accessibility work to get through
  review. C takes width away from a table that already has six columns.

  Have a look and tell me what you think here. You can click an option in the browser to select it.

  One housekeeping note: the repo has no [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m, and the sketches are saved under [38;5;153m.hyperpowers/[39m. That folder should
  be ignored. I won't add a [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m without your go-ahead, since it's outside this task.

